[
  "ACT 1: COLD OPEN & PERSONAL GROUNDING [00:00 - 03:00]\nScene: 01. Starting Soon -> 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nWelcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The AI Horizon & The Observable Control Plane. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers in Chicago were building grassroots rooms to escape corporate silos. Today we rewatch Episode 33: Stuart Halloway from SCNA 2013 (2013).",
  "ACT 2: SETTING THE HISTORICAL SCENE [03:00 - 08:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nStuart Halloway's SCNA presence connected the Chicago craftsmanship community with the emerging functional programming renaissance. When we recorded this in 2013, there were no corporate sponsor filters. Developers were meeting after hours, sharing hard-won lessons on deliberate practice and system boundaries.",
  "ACT 3: THE CORE INQUIRY: THE SOUND ABOVE [08:00 - 14:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera -> 04. Split Screen\n\nWhy did Clojure and Datomic capture the imagination of Midwest craftsmen seeking refuge from object-oriented ceremonies? Who inspired Stuart Halloway before they stepped onto this stage? What records were playing in the background when this movement formed?",
  "ACT 4: HALLWAY REWATCH & VIDEO REACTION [14:00 - 28:00]\nScene: 03. Reaction - Video Focus\n\nRoll archive footage (YouTube ID: eJtP70a6c2E). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "ACT 5: THE AI-ERA PARALLEL & TERMINAL WORKBENCH [28:00 - 40:00]\nScene: 05. Workbench - Code & Terminal\n\nImmutable append-only facts and temporal event logs are the foundation of observable agent telemetries and memory layers. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "ACT 6: COMMUNITY CODA, OUTRO & NEXT STREAM [40:00 - 45:00]\nScene: 08. Outro & Next Stream\n\nThank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 34. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]